    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "AIDS",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "Reports of success with protease inhibitor-based HAART are appearing at the same time as reports of puzzling metabolic effects. These effects include loss of peripheral subcutaneous fat, truncal obesity, hyperlipidemia, and frank diabetes. There is no consensus on how often these problems manifest themselves. Patients taking protease inhibitors (PIs) also appear to be at higher risk of developing coronary disease, although more study is needed. Another question explored is whether PI-related complications can be reversed."
    }
